Temperature and Humidity Monitoring with LED Control

Aim

To monitor room temperature and humidity using ESP32 and DHT11 sensor and control a red LED through a web page.

Components Required

- ESP32 Development Board
- DHT11 Sensor
- Red LED
- 220Ω Resistor
- Jumper Wires
- USB Cable

Connections

Component| ESP32 Pin
DHT11 DATA| GPIO 4
DHT11 VCC| 3.3V
DHT11 GND| GND
Red LED| GPIO 2

Software Requirements

- Arduino IDE
- ESP32 Board Package
- DHT Sensor Library
- Adafruit Unified Sensor Library

Working

1. ESP32 connects to Wi-Fi.
2. DHT11 measures temperature and humidity.
3. Sensor values are displayed on a web page.
4. The user can turn the red LED ON using the web page.
5. The user can turn the red LED OFF using the web page.
6. Temperature and humidity values update every 2 seconds.

Features

- Real-time temperature monitoring
- Humidity monitoring
- Red LED ON/OFF control
- Wi-Fi-based web interface
- Mobile phone access

Applications

- Smart Home Monitoring
- Room Temperature Monitoring
- IoT Automation
- Smart Lighting Systems

Conclusion

This project demonstrates how ESP32 and DHT11 can be used to monitor temperature and humidity and control an LED remotely through a Wi-Fi-based web interface.
